-- hand-edit this file.
--
-- ⚠ THIS HALF CANNOT BE DRY-RUN ALONE -- its chamber hangs off a government the
--   structure half creates. Run all three halves as ONE transaction ending in
--   ROLLBACK and assert the stream holds zero executable COMMIT beforehand.
--   🔴 Assert on `^\s*COMMIT\s*;`, NOT on a substring count: this file contains
--   the word "commit" legitimately, in prose and in ON COMMIT DROP.
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 🔴🔴 CONSOLIDATION MERGES THE LEGISLATIVE BODY ONLY. THERE IS NO COMMISSION
--      HERE, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE DIFFERENCE FROM BALDWIN.
--
-- The Columbus Council IS the county legislature, so stage 4 drops the county
-- commission entirely and keeps only the separately elected county officers.
-- This chamber therefore attaches to the SAME government row the structure half
-- created -- one government, three chambers.
--
-- 🔴 EVERY COUNT IN THE POST-VERIFY IS SCOPED TO THIS ONE CHAMBER, never to the
--    government. A government-wide count here would couple this migration to the
--    city halves in both directions.
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 🔴 RULING R4 (Cantrell, 2026-09-01): FIVE OFFICERS. BALDWIN'S TEMPLATE DOES
--    NOT TRANSFER, WHICH IS EXACTLY WHAT "CONFIRM FROM THE CHARTER, INHERIT
--    NOTHING" EXISTS TO CATCH.
--
-- Charter Article VIII, Chapter 1 "County Officers and Agencies" preserves four
-- offices through consolidation: Sec. 8-100 Sheriff, 8-101 Judge of Probate
-- Court, 8-102 Tax Commissioner, 8-103 Coroner. The Clerk of Superior Court is
-- not in Article VIII because it does not need to be -- Ga. Const. Art. IX,
-- Sec. I, Par. III names it a county officer and attaches it to a state court,
-- and consolidation cannot reach it.
--
-- 🔴 MUSCOGEE ELECTS NO MARSHAL AND NO SURVEYOR. Baldwin elected both and was
--    seated with six officers one wave ago.
--
-- EXCLUDED, each for a stated reason:
--   Solicitor General              a prosecutor -- the FL-5 rule against Palm
--                                  Beach's State Attorney, and Baldwin's
--   District Attorney, Chattahoochee  MULTI-COUNTY circuit -- the FL-5 ruling
--   Municipal Court Clerk and Judge   ✅ RULED 2026-09-01 (Cantrell): EXCLUDE
--                                  BOTH. A municipal court is a Ga. Const.
--                                  Art. VI court, the same line Baldwin drew for
--                                  the Chief Magistrate. ⚠ The counter-argument
--                                  -- that Muscogee voters genuinely elect both
--                                  countywide -- is recorded, not dropped:
--                                  Macon-Bibb, Philadelphia and Lexington will
--                                  each raise it again.
--   Clerk of Council               appointed by the Council, Sec. 3-103(1)
--   School Board, Soil and Water   spec §11
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 🔴 THE COUNTYWIDE DISTRICT IS ASSERTED, NEVER CREATED.
--
-- The TIGER county load already made 13215/G4020 a COUNTY district -- verified
-- in production 2026-09-01: 1 row, carrying 0 offices. Inserting it again would
-- lay a second district over the same ground. The pre-flight FAILS HARD if it is
-- missing: the five officers have nowhere to sit without it.
--
-- ⚠ It covers the SAME 221.011 sq mi as the citywide LOCAL district the
--   structure half created. That is correct and unavoidable under consolidation:
--   same ground, two tiers. The post-verify asserts the tiers were not crossed.
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 🟢 THE CHANGE-CHECK WAS RUN LIVE ON 2026-09-01 AND IT ASKED "HAS THIS PERSON
--    LEFT?". IT PRODUCED FIVE NAME CORRECTIONS AND ONE STATED GAP.
--
--   Sheriff       Greg Countryman        his own office: "Sheriff Greg
--                                        Countryman" and, once, "Gregory D.
--                                        Countryman". 🔴 NO "Sr." ANYWHERE --
--                                        the suffix in the first draft was
--                                        unsourced and is dropped.
--   Clerk         Danielle F. Forté      her own office writes "Meet Danielle F.
--                                        Forté", WITH the accent. The certified
--                                        ballot writes the ASCII form, kept as
--                                        an alias.
--   Tax Comm.     David A. Britt II      his own office: "David A. Britt II,
--                                        MBA, MPA". The ballot said "David
--                                        Britt".
--   Coroner       Buddy Bryan            the Georgia Coroners Association
--                                        directory names him "Eddie Bryan" and
--                                        Ballotpedia "Eddie Lynwood Bryan" --
--                                        SAME PERSON, same seat, same office
--                                        address. "Buddy" is the ballot and
--                                        press name and stays the full_name.
--                                        ⚠ He pronounced a death on 2026-08-31,
--                                        which is the freshest occupancy
--                                        evidence in the wave.
--   Probate Judge Marc D'Antonio         ⚠ THE ONE SEAT WHOSE CHANGE-CHECK COULD
--                                        NOT REACH 2026 -- see below.
--
-- ⚠ THE PROBATE JUDGE'S NEWEST POSITIVE EVIDENCE IS 2025-01-13, AND THAT LIMIT
--   IS STATED RATHER THAN HIDDEN. His court's own website never names its judge
--   (measured twice, including JS-rendered); gaprobate.gov's directory would not
--   filter to a county; Ballotpedia has no Muscogee County officials page at all
--   -- "Muscogee County, Georgia" redirects to the city page, which carries only
--   federal, state and city seats. What stands: the certified 2024 return, and
--   his court's own 2025 fee schedule, authored "Marc D'Antonio" and created
--   2025-01-13, which is AFTER he took office. Nothing anywhere reports a
--   departure. 🔴 That is not the same as currency -- it is exactly the shape of
--   the Baldwin coroner failure, where every source agreed and all of them
--   predated the retirement. Re-check this seat at GA-5.
--
-- ⚠ "Having served in the office for 25 years" on the Tax Commissioner's bio is
--   service in the DEPARTMENT, not tenure in the elected seat. He became Tax
--   Commissioner in 2025, succeeding Lula Huff, who did not seek re-election.
--   Reading the 25 years as occupancy would be the published-expiry error class.
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 🔴 4 TERMS ARE OPEN-ENDED AT 'unknown'; 1 IS DATED AT 'month'.
--
-- Britt took office when Huff's term expired at the end of 2024. The MONTH is
-- sourced; the day is not, so precision is 'month' and 2025-01-01 is a
-- placeholder the precision disclaims. The other four have no published
-- service-start of any kind, and re-election does not restart occupancy.
--
-- IDEMPOTENT: every insert is NOT EXISTS-guarded or ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, the
-- occupancy loop skips any office+politician pair that already has a term row,
-- and every assertion is a statement about the END STATE.

BEGIN;

-- --- 0. Pre-flight ----------------------------------------------------------
-- 🔴 THIS MIGRATION CREATES NO GOVERNMENT AND NO DISTRICT. Both must already
-- exist, and their ABSENCE is a hard stop rather than something to insert
-- around.
DO $$
DECLARE v_n int;
BEGIN
  IF NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM essentials.governments WHERE geo_id = '1319000' AND type = 'City'
  ) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'muscogee county: the Columbus Consolidated Government, Georgia, US row is missing -- apply the city structure half first';
  END IF;

  -- ⚠ ALWAYS PAIR geo_id WITH mtfcc AND district_type. Georgia's collision is
  -- THREE-WAY, and this wave carries a LOCAL district over the SAME ground as
  -- this COUNTY one -- so district_type is the only thing separating the tiers.
  IF NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM essentials.geofence_boundaries
     WHERE geo_id = '13215' AND mtfcc = 'G4020'
  ) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'muscogee county: boundary 13215/G4020 is missing -- the TIGER county load must be applied first';
  END IF;

  SELECT count(*) INTO v_n FROM essentials.districts
   WHERE geo_id = '13215' AND mtfcc = 'G4020'
     AND district_type = 'COUNTY' AND lower(state) = 'ga';
  IF v_n <> 1 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'muscogee county: expected exactly 1 existing G4020 COUNTY district 13215, found % -- this migration does not create it', v_n;
  END IF;
END $$;

-- --- 1. Chamber -------------------------------------------------------------
-- ⚠ chambers.slug is GENERATED from name_formal and cannot be inserted.
-- ⚠ The name carries "Muscogee County" rather than Baldwin's bare "Elected
-- Officials", because under consolidation this chamber shares a government row
-- with two CITY chambers and a bare name would read as the city's.

INSERT INTO essentials.chambers
  (government_id, name, name_formal, official_count, policy_engagement_level)
SELECT g.id, 'Muscogee County Elected Officials', 'Muscogee County Elected Officials', 5, 'full'
FROM essentials.governments g
WHERE g.geo_id = '1319000' AND g.type = 'City'
  AND NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM essentials.chambers c WHERE c.government_id = g.id AND c.name = 'Muscogee County Elected Officials'
  );

-- --- 2. Offices -------------------------------------------------------------
-- ⚠ representing_city is NULL: these are COUNTY officers, following Baldwin
-- (CC_0029). Under consolidation they serve the same ground as the city, but
-- the seat is a county seat and the column should not imply otherwise.

INSERT INTO essentials.offices
  (chamber_id, district_id, title, representing_state, representing_city, voting_powers)
SELECT c.id, d.id, 'Sheriff', 'GA', NULL, 'full'
FROM essentials.chambers c
JOIN essentials.governments g ON g.id = c.government_id
CROSS JOIN LATERAL (
  SELECT dd.id FROM essentials.districts dd
   WHERE dd.geo_id = '13215' AND dd.mtfcc = 'G4020'
     AND dd.district_type = 'COUNTY' AND lower(dd.state) = 'ga'
) d
WHERE g.geo_id = '1319000' AND g.type = 'City' AND c.name = 'Muscogee County Elected Officials'
  AND NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM essentials.offices o
    WHERE o.chamber_id = c.id AND o.district_id = d.id AND o.title = 'Sheriff'
  );
INSERT INTO essentials.offices
  (chamber_id, district_id, title, representing_state, representing_city, voting_powers)
SELECT c.id, d.id, 'Clerk of Superior Court', 'GA', NULL, 'full'
FROM essentials.chambers c
JOIN essentials.governments g ON g.id = c.government_id
CROSS JOIN LATERAL (
  SELECT dd.id FROM essentials.districts dd
   WHERE dd.geo_id = '13215' AND dd.mtfcc = 'G4020'
     AND dd.district_type = 'COUNTY' AND lower(dd.state) = 'ga'
) d
WHERE g.geo_id = '1319000' AND g.type = 'City' AND c.name = 'Muscogee County Elected Officials'
  AND NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM essentials.offices o
    WHERE o.chamber_id = c.id AND o.district_id = d.id AND o.title = 'Clerk of Superior Court'
  );
INSERT INTO essentials.offices
  (chamber_id, district_id, title, representing_state, representing_city, voting_powers)
SELECT c.id, d.id, 'Judge of Probate Court', 'GA', NULL, 'full'
FROM essentials.chambers c
JOIN essentials.governments g ON g.id = c.government_id
CROSS JOIN LATERAL (
  SELECT dd.id FROM essentials.districts dd
   WHERE dd.geo_id = '13215' AND dd.mtfcc = 'G4020'
     AND dd.district_type = 'COUNTY' AND lower(dd.state) = 'ga'
) d
WHERE g.geo_id = '1319000' AND g.type = 'City' AND c.name = 'Muscogee County Elected Officials'
  AND NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM essentials.offices o
    WHERE o.chamber_id = c.id AND o.district_id = d.id AND o.title = 'Judge of Probate Court'
  );
INSERT INTO essentials.offices
  (chamber_id, district_id, title, representing_state, representing_city, voting_powers)
SELECT c.id, d.id, 'Tax Commissioner', 'GA', NULL, 'full'
FROM essentials.chambers c
JOIN essentials.governments g ON g.id = c.government_id
CROSS JOIN LATERAL (
  SELECT dd.id FROM essentials.districts dd
   WHERE dd.geo_id = '13215' AND dd.mtfcc = 'G4020'
     AND dd.district_type = 'COUNTY' AND lower(dd.state) = 'ga'
) d
WHERE g.geo_id = '1319000' AND g.type = 'City' AND c.name = 'Muscogee County Elected Officials'
  AND NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM essentials.offices o
    WHERE o.chamber_id = c.id AND o.district_id = d.id AND o.title = 'Tax Commissioner'
  );
INSERT INTO essentials.offices
  (chamber_id, district_id, title, representing_state, representing_city, voting_powers)
SELECT c.id, d.id, 'Coroner', 'GA', NULL, 'full'
FROM essentials.chambers c
JOIN essentials.governments g ON g.id = c.government_id
CROSS JOIN LATERAL (
  SELECT dd.id FROM essentials.districts dd
   WHERE dd.geo_id = '13215' AND dd.mtfcc = 'G4020'
     AND dd.district_type = 'COUNTY' AND lower(dd.state) = 'ga'
) d
WHERE g.geo_id = '1319000' AND g.type = 'City' AND c.name = 'Muscogee County Elected Officials'
  AND NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM essentials.offices o
    WHERE o.chamber_id = c.id AND o.district_id = d.id AND o.title = 'Coroner'
